> Trace the executed compact architecture

A conditioner stores 16 hidden weights, 16 hidden biases, 16 output weights and
one output bias: 49 values. Four conditioners give 196; log_scale adds two.
The total is **198 values in 17 tensors**. Hidden weights use normal standard
deviation .3 and bias .05; shift heads use deviation .01 and zero bias. Native
seed 9301 initializes the warmed forward store in block order, then scale zero.
The original optional TensorFlow initial-array directory is absent, so its
auto default selects this native initialization. The following graph groups
two executed couplings per stage for readable labels; it counts real leaves.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nice_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(9301);
 n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){auto o=n::models::NiceDensity(p,x);
  n::model_stage("Additive stages 0 / 1",x,o.coupling1);
  n::model_stage("Additive stages 2 / 3",o.coupling1,o.unscaled);
  return n::model_stage("Positive diagonal scale",o.unscaled,o.latent);
 },"NICE: 198 values / 17 leaves");
 n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=2;
 auto figure=model.plot(n::zeros({1,2}),options);
 if(figure.parameter_count()!=198||p.size()!=17)throw std::runtime_error("Executed NICE census");
 figure.save_svg("build/nice_network.svg");
}
```
