> Check actual forward and inverse determinants at every original point

Reverse-mode differentiation of each output coordinate yields the two actual
Jacobian rows. Their positive determinant agrees with exp(sum(log_scale)) for
all 128 held-out points and its reciprocal for all 1,024 inverse samples.
The following plot retains all 1,152 log determinants, subtracting the analytic
value and scaling differences by 1e7 so Float32 errors are visible. A zero
residual verifies the global volume factor; it does not imply constant Jacobian
entries or a linear map.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nice_jacobians.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> v,o;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/nice_density/plot_values.npz"))v[k]=x;
 for(auto& [k,x]:n::load_npz("build/nice_density/outputs.npz"))o[k]=x;
 double ld=o.at("forward_logdet").item();auto a=(v.at("actual_logdet")-ld)*1e7,b=(v.at("inverse_actual_logdet")+ld)*1e7;
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.points(n::arange(0,128).to_vector<double>(),a.to_vector<double>(),"Forward, all128 test rows",{37,99,235},3)
 .points(n::arange(0,1024).to_vector<double>(),b.to_vector<double>(),"Inverse, all1024 prior rows",{234,88,12},2)
 .y_limits(-3,5).x_label("Row index in its own pool").y_label("(Actual - analytic logdet) x 1e7")
 .title("Actual Jacobians match the global volume factor within Float32")
 .save_svg("build/nice_jacobians.svg");
}
```
