| forward(inverse(prior)) |2.38418579102e-07|
| Change-of-variables log identity |1.53024113914e-06|
\image(figures/nice_normalization.svg)
// result_end

\caption(All 1,024 normalization residuals are plotted in original prior-row order, without subsampling. The checks also include bit-exact restore, repeated samples/Jacobians, single/batch parity and immutable inference.)
\alttext(1024 blue absolute normalization residuals remain small at the displayed million-fold scale; no row exceeds the original 2e-5-nat tolerance.)

> What the checks establish

The original procedural pools, all learned states/gradients, all 48 Adam writes,
three validation records, actual forward/inverse Jacobians, every prior sample,
density grid, fitting-only moments and source scalar metrics reproduce exactly.
The independent NumPy audit composes analytic triangular Jacobian matrices,
checks all 17 parameter leaves by finite differences, verifies every captured
update and every inverse sample, and independently reconstructs the raw MT
Box-Muller banks. It does not call native model math or refit a substitute.

This compact experiment demonstrates exact-form inversion and tractable
likelihood with a global volume factor. It does not demonstrate superior test
density: the final NICE score is slightly worse than either fitted Gaussian
baseline. All 198 parameters, the original seeds and the predefined final epoch
are retained. A different conditioner, longer schedule, alternate base or
validation-selected fit would be a different experiment requiring its own study.

